#X restore 900 330 pd regions;
#X text 900 430 THE FILL IS THE CLEAR. Every frame writes all 99 cells before anything else \, so there is no separate blank step to forget and no way for a stale pad to survive a layer change. t b b f sets the colour into its cold store FIRST \, off the rightmost outlet \, then resets the counter \, then runs the loop., f 50;
#X text 900 600 The counter reset is a message box into the cold inlet off the trigger's rightmost outlet \, so a loop can never start from wherever the last one stopped -- the reset-to-23 lesson from u_tempo \, in its simplest form., f 50;
#X connect 1 0 4 0;
#X connect 2 0 5 0;
#X connect 3 0 7 0;
#X connect 4 0 9 0;
#X connect 5 0 9 0;
#X connect 6 0 5 1;
#X connect 7 1 8 0;
#X connect 7 0 19 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 2 10 1;
#X connect 9 1 18 0;
#X connect 9 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 13 0 15 0;
#X connect 14 0 13 1;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 1 17 1;
#X connect 16 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 17 0;
#X connect 18 0 13 1;
#X restore 20 1580 pd prepare;
#X text 280 1614 fills the frame buffer from whichever layer won -- emits nothing, f 50;
#N canvas 30 30 2000 1150 paint 0;
#X text 20 20 THE ONLY THING IN Cut It THAT SENDS TO THESE LEDs. One SysEx per repaint \, carrying the whole span: the header \, then 99 times a type byte \, an index and a colour \, then 247., f 58;
#X text 20 140 THE SPAN IS 10 TO 108 \, AND THAT IS A MEASURED CEILING RATHER THAN A TIDY ROUND NUMBER. 99 specs in one message is accepted on this unit \; 120 is REJECTED OUTRIGHT -- the whole message is dropped rather than truncated \, so an over-long frame would show up as the grid silently freezing. 10 to 108 covers the 8x8 grid \, both side columns \, the top row and the lower of the two bottom rows. THE EIGHT BUTTONS AT INDEX 1 TO 8 ARE DELIBERATELY OUTSIDE IT: lighting those as well would put the count at about 106 \, which is the documented limit and far too close to a cliff that fails silently., f 58;
#X obj 20 420 inlet;
#X obj 20 480 t b b b b;
#X msg 20 560 247;
#X obj 20 620 s \$0-byte;
#X msg 300 560 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 3;
#X obj 300 620 s \$0-byte;
#X msg 700 480 0;
#X msg 900 560 99;
#X obj 900 620 until;
#X obj 900 680 f;
#X obj 1060 740 + 1;
#X obj 900 740 + 10;
#X obj 900 800 t f f b;
#X msg 1320 870 0;
#X obj 1320 930 s \$0-byte;
#X obj 1120 870 s \$0-byte;
#X obj 900 870 tabread \$0-surface;
#X obj 900 930 s \$0-byte;
#X text 20 1000 t f f b EMITS THE THREE BYTES OF A SPEC IN THE RIGHT ORDER BY FIRING RIGHT TO LEFT: the type \, then the index \, then the colour read back out of the buffer. Taking that order from one trigger rather than from three separate chains is what makes it impossible to send a spec with its bytes swapped., f 90;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 3 8 0;
#X connect 3 2 6 0;
#X connect 3 1 9 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 11 1;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 11 0 13 0;
#X connect 12 0 11 1;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 2 15 0;
#X connect 14 1 17 0;
#X connect 14 0 18 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 18 0 19 0;
#X restore 700 1660 pd paint;
#X text 960 1694 one SysEx \, 99 specs \, indices 10 to 108, f 50;
#X obj 1500 780 loadbang;
#X obj 1500 840 del 400;
#X obj 1500 890 metro 100;
#X obj 1500 950 f;
#X obj 1660 910 r \$0-dirty;
#X obj 1500 1010 select 1;
#X obj 1500 1070 spigot;
#X obj 1740 1030 r \$0-own;
#X obj 1500 1130 t b b b;
#X msg 1740 1190 0;
#X obj 1740 1250 s \$0-dirty;
#X obj 2100 780 r \$0-byte;
#X obj 2100 900 midiout;
#X obj 2280 840 f \$1;
#X obj 2280 780 loadbang;
#X text 1500 1330 THE FRAME CLOCK RUNS AT 10 Hz BUT REPAINTS ONLY WHEN DIRTY \, and that is the one place this file must NOT copy g_oled. The OLED redraws unconditionally because its frames are cheap UDP to a local socket. These are ALSA MIDI writes \, and about 96 of those a second is the standing suspect for the clock roughly doubling Pd's CPU in Phase 5 -- so an unconditional full-surface repaint at 10 Hz would add to exactly the cost that already hurts. Idle with the transport stopped this sends NOTHING AT ALL. At 120 BPM the beat row moves twice a second \, so it sends twice a second., f 90;
#X text 1500 1520 THE SPIGOT COMES BEFORE THE FLAG IS CLEARED \, deliberately. While the surface is not ours the flag stays set \, so whatever changed while a stock layout had the pads gets painted in the first frame after we get them back rather than being lost., f 90;
#X text 2100 990 THE PORT IS AN OBJECT-BOX \$1 \, NOT A MESSAGE-BOX ONE. In a message box \$1 is the first element of the incoming message and would resolve to 0 \, which is a different port and a silent one. Same glyph \, unrelated meaning -- ref-conventions.md \, The \$1 trap., f 50;
